# Design handoff

- Follow the user's latest visual requirements. Existing design tokens and components guide implementation but do not override an explicitly requested measurement or behavior.
- Inspect the relevant component and design/screenshot before changing layout. Distinguish measured values from estimates.
- Reuse semantic colors, typography, and existing primitives where they fit. Do not round a requested value to a spacing grid without a reason.
- Preserve keyboard/focus behavior, text overflow, and theme compatibility while matching the requested design.
- Verify visually at the relevant size and state. Report screenshot-based comparison or missing browser/Figma access accurately.
